<title>GERMANY: West German March industry orders rise 0.7 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>West German March industry orders rise 0.7 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Mar 97     Feb 97	Mar 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +0.7	 -0.6	  +1.5</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+4.5	 +5.3	  -2.9</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		 97.6	 96.9	  93.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				   Mar 97   Feb 97   Mar 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders		+0.5     +0.6	86.9</p>
<p> Foreign orders		 +1.1     -2.4     118.8</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	   +0.8     +2.3     100.5</p>
<p> Capital goods		  +0.1     +2.3	90.8</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables   +2.2     +1.6     122.5</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Feb/Mar 97 with Dec/Jan 96/97:  Industrial orders		    +1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Feb/Mar 97 with Feb/Mar 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +0.4</p>
<p> Domestic orders			-2.6</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +5.1</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +4.6</p>
<p> Capital goods			  -4.2</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	   -1.0</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
